    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0255" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.24/232a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-08T18:00:00-04:00">August 8, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>205. Your 250 and 251, August 5.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d269-f1"/> The Iranian
                    Minister here has reached an agreement with Joseph P. Sheridan for the latter’s
                    appointment as Food and Supply Adviser to the Iranian Government. Minister has
                    cabled Tehran for approval of the terms agreed upon. Because of the various
                    inoculations required for air travel to the Near East, Sheridan will necessarily
                    be delayed here until early <pb facs="0256" n="244" xml:id="pg244"/> September,
                    but it is hoped he will be able to depart for Tehran immediately after September
                    7.</p>
                <p>In your discretion you may inform the Prime Minister<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d269-f2"/> that the Department considers Sheridan a very able man
                    and believes that if given full cooperation by the Iranian Government he will be
                    of great assistance in solving the pressing supply problems confronting Iran.
                    During his stay in Washington he will make a study of the situation in so far as
                    information is available here and will investigate the questions involved in
                    obtaining supplies from the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
